    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "45c8ff49618c8769114b74b83895ed6a3a425340",
      "message": "OTA-1866 \u2014 a question is asked once\n\n#191. Owner's contract for a vendor conversation: a question is asked\nonce, the answer lands once, the conversation remembers it, and the\nquestion is not offered again for that character.\n\nMEASURED VIOLATION, bundle muc6fh1tj2l7 of 2026-09-22: 79 asks in 25.1s\nagainst Ilva Sidelong, three rotating options, \"I have told you that\none.\" every time, ~200ms apart, input healthy, conversation exited\nnormally. Ilva is roadside:ilva_sidelong -> class:roadside, and the\nthree labels in the trace are exactly that class's topics open at\nfamiliar regard: c_front / c_known / cls_roadside_pitch.\n\nCLASS ERROR, NOT AN ILVA ONE \u2014 and not where the symptom pointed. The\nengine was right throughout. OTA-1784 made a class set's lines PARALLEL\nVOICES (one answer per person, not a repeat sequence) and introduced\nanswersAvailable to say so; raiseTopic's already-said guard and\nhasUnspokenTalk's glow were both moved onto it, the glow's own comment\nreading \"on lines.length a laned trader's glow never dims\". TalkSheet\nwas not moved. It kept asking talked >= topic.lines.length.\n\nFor class:roadside \u2014 six lanes per topic \u2014 that is 1 >= 6, false. And\npermanently false: raiseTopic returns on the already-said path BEFORE\nthe counter write, so the counter freezes at 1 and can never reach 6.\nThe row stayed undimmed, unsunk, unlabelled and pressable for the rest\nof that character's life. 79 presses is only how long the owner kept\npressing.\n\nCENSUS (41 topic sets: 30 authored NPCs, 11 class sets; 347 topics).\nclass:roadside is the ONLY set where the two readers disagree: its six\ntopics carry six lines each, while every other class set has one line\nper topic (1 >= 1 agrees) and an authored set's answersAvailable IS\nlines.length (agrees by construction). 6 questions violating, 1 set, 0\nidentity collisions, 0 duplicate ids within a set, 0 unstable ids.\n\nREPAIR \u2014 one authority, not a patch per reader. topicSpent(topic,\nnpcId, talked) lives beside answersAvailable; the store's guard, the\nTALK glow and the topic list all ask it. It takes the topic and the\nperson rather than a caller-supplied count, so a reader cannot pass the\nwrong number any more: the divergence is made unrepresentable rather\nthan corrected twice and hoped about.\n\nNOT A RACE, and proven so rather than assumed: raiseTopic latches the\ncounter synchronously inside the call that accepts the selection, so 50\nback-to-back presses in one tick yield exactly one authored answer\nbefore and after the repair. Rapid pressing exposed the defect; a\ndebounce would not have touched it.\n\nDialogue text, authored answers, gates, grants, flourishes, vendor\ninventory, prices, standing and navigation are untouched. No line of\nauthored prose changed.\n\nNEW SUITE ota1866TheQuestionIsAskedOnce 24/24 \u2014 corpus identity, the\nask-once lifecycle driven through raiseTopic for all 41 sets, the\nrendered TalkSheet tray for a laned multi-line class / a laned\nsingle-line class / an authored person, reopen, save round-trip, legacy\nsaves starting clean, cross-vendor and cross-character isolation, the\ngrant-idempotency check, and the Ilva fixture including the 79-press\ndevice loop. Eight of the 24 were red before the repair and the two\nalready-agreeing classes were green, which is what isolated the class.\n\nNEGATIVE CONTROLS: consumed-state filtering removed -> 11 red; vendor\nidentity dropped from the key -> 11 red; save/load dropping the memory\n-> 1 red. Production was restored, not left patched. The brief's fourth\ncontrol (state written after narration rather than at acceptance) does\nnot apply: timing is not part of the proven defect.\n\nALSO CORRECTED: ota1865's own build-stamp pin, which asserted the live\nOTA_BUILD_ID and so went red on the next OTA for no defect. check:otastamp\nalready ties the stamp to the newest suite and is a gate, not a test.\n\nGates: typecheck:ci clean, typecheck:tests 196 baseline no growth, lint\nclean, 22/22 check:* (storeceiling at 36815, quotedpins 112/112), fast\nsurface 1364/1364 suites, 15,666 passed / 3 skipped, exit 0. No Heavy.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: anything about NPC conversation outside the sets this same\nmachinery governs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
